    "result_text": "The only concrete test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes. Build is green.\n\nThe change is complete. Summary of what I implemented, following the existing duplicate-telephone/household pattern in this Spring Boot app:\n\n1. **`DuplicateEmailException`** (`service/`) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` thrown by the service layer, mirroring `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 added a guard for new owners: if the owner's email is already used by any existing owner (compared case-insensitively on its lower-cased form), it throws `DuplicateEmailException`. The helper `isEmailAlreadyUsed` treats a null/blank email as non-colliding, so emailless owners (the default `ownerNode()` payload) are unaffected.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` mapping `DuplicateEmailException` to **409 Conflict**, consistent with the other duplicate handlers.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` (create an owner with a unique email, then a second owner with the same email \u2192 expect 409) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
