    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, additive extension that mirrors the codebase's established patterns:\n\n- **`DuplicateEmailException`** sits in the service package alongside the sibling exceptions (`DuplicateTelephoneException`, `DuplicateHouseholdException`, etc.), extends `RuntimeException`, and carries a message-building constructor exactly like them.\n- **The service check** is inserted as another `owner.isNew() && \u2026` guard in `saveOwner`, in the natural spot next to the telephone check, keeping the uniqueness invariant in the service layer where the others live.\n- **`isEmailAlreadyUsed`** is placed among the other private helpers and deliberately follows the same `ownerRepository.findAll().stream()` + case-insensitive idiom as its immediate neighbors `countNamesakes` and `findHouseholdMembers`, so the in-memory approach is consistent rather than an outlier (not a repository `existsBy\u2026` call, but that matches how these case-insensitive checks are already done here).\n- **The exception handler** is a faithful copy of the surrounding handlers' shape (warn-log, `CONFLICT` status, `detailBuild`, `ResponseEntity`), inserted in a sensible order.\n\nLogic is in the right unit, nothing is duplicated beyond the intentional idiom-matching, and no class is turning into a catch-all. A maintainer would find this natural.",
